{"name":"Erin","hex":"#00ff40","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Erin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Ireland.","A female personification of Ireland, in the manner of Britannia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Erin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erin","blocks":[{"text":"Erin is a personal name taken from the Hiberno-English word for Ireland, originating from the Irish word \"Éirinn\". \"Éirinn\" is the dative case of the Irish word for Ireland, \"Éire\", genitive \"Éireann\", the dative being used in prepositional phrases such as \"go hÉirinn\" \"to Ireland\", \"in Éirinn\" \"in Ireland\", \"ó Éirinn\" \"from Ireland\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Topography_Ireland.jpg/330px-Topography_Ireland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erin","wikidata":"Q770100"},{"title":"Shades of green","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color green may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a green or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Shades_of_Green.svg/330px-Shades_of_Green.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_green","wikidata":"Q19847180"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/RGB_illumination.jpg/330px-RGB_illumination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/RGB_illumination.jpg/330px-RGB_illumination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red, green and blue lights, representing the three bas